      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilson_Creek%2C_Washington",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A railroad reached the area in 1892, anchoring the town’s growth along the Great Northern Railway line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilson_Creek%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Wilson Creek serves as the unofficial gateway to the dramatic Channeled Scablands of the Columbia Basin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://scientificmagz.blog/wilson-creek-wa-history-scablands",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Nearby Billy Clapp Lake and Pinto Dam, part of the Columbia Basin Project, lie just west of town along Crab Creek.",
